# 01-scenery-rows: the parallax layers and the ground filled a word (8 pixels) at a time instead of a nibble at a time.
#
# On the board the scenery is drawn a column at a time (drawLayerCols, drawGroundCols: colFill, colTex, colPair), each
# pixel a read-modify-write of a byte at stride 64. On the GBA that was half of the frame. This patch renames the two
# game functions to old_drawLayerCols / old_drawGroundCols (kept for the GBA_SCENECHECK build, otherwise unused and
# dropped by the compiler) and includes scenery_rows.inc, which defines new ones drawing the same picture in 8-column
# strips, row by row, with whole-word writes. Their callers (drawWorld, drawTitleScene) come later in the file and so
# get the new ones. A line in buildTile tells them when the texture changed (they keep it by rows).

